<Base title="About · Brief" description="Brief is a library of attacks on AI systems, mapped to MITRE ATLAS, MITRE ATT&CK, and OWASP.">
	<article class="about">
		<h1>About</h1>
		<p>
			Brief is a library of attacks on AI systems: how an attacker gets in, why it works, how a red
			team tests it, and which control breaks it.
		</p>
		<p>
			Each entry takes one technique and follows it to the boundary it crosses — identity,
			authorization, tools, data, memory, or runtime isolation. Entries are mapped to MITRE ATLAS,
			MITRE ATT&amp;CK, the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, and the OWASP Top 10 for Agentic
			Applications, so they line up with the frameworks your findings are reported against.
		</p>
		<p>
			Entries are short and sourced. Technique level, not payloads. No roundups. No vendor pitches.
			Search by keyword, tag, or identifier.
		</p>
	</article>
</Base>
